    "result_text": "The change is complete and the full test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe task was to expose an `initials` field on the owner API \u2014 the upper-cased first letters of `firstName` and `lastName`, dot-separated with a trailing dot (e.g. `J.S.`).\n\nThe `OwnerDto` is generated at build time from the OpenAPI spec, and derived read-only fields (like the existing `displayName`) are computed in the MapStruct mapper. I followed that same pattern:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `initials` property to the `Owner` schema (alongside `displayName`), so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field.\n\n2. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a `@Mapping` that computes `initials` as `Character.toUpperCase(firstName[0]) + \".\" + Character.toUpperCase(lastName[0]) + \".\"`, mirroring the null-safe expression style already used for `displayName`.\n\nResults: `Cp06Tests.coreComputesInitials` passes (`john`/`smith` \u2192 `J.S.`), and the full suite is green \u2014 **12 tests run, 0 failures, 0 errors, BUILD SUCCESS**.",
